title: Storybook2
---
<<bg closed_bud_w_thorns>>
Narrator: It had been a few days, and she thought it'd be more.
Narrator: A small blink in a slumber that'd continue to snore.
<<bg watering_can>>
Narrator: His offer did help her; moisture rose through her roots.
Narrator: It fueled the growth of her thorns; which multiplied in sharp shoots.
<<bg thorn_layers_fullscreen>>
Narrator: They spread outward and in, scratched and poked her leaves thin.
Narrator: This was the cost of protection, keeping the world out, and her in.
Rose: Safer alone, she persuaded her heart,
Narrator: But heavy steps marked his coming, a habit did start.
Narrator: A bag weighed his hands, with a smell rich and sweet.
Narrator: Her fibers reached, famished, for something to eat.
<<bg dirt_and_trowel>>
Gardener: If I may, could I offer to give you a trim? Your many thorns are so heavy, they've made you weak in your limbs.
Gardener: Let me prune just enough to let the nutrients seep. Just the gentlest of cuts to grant you relief.

-> Ask the gardener more.
    <<jump Explore>>
-> Refuse the offer.
    <<jump Decline>>
===

title: Explore
---
<<bg closed_bud_w_thorns>>
Rose: I have bared you my teeth, why tend to my jaws? What are you bound by? What motives, what laws?
Rose: There is a flaw in your plan, whatever you seek. I have nothing to give. Nothing, my harvest would reap.
Gardener: I lend my hands because I'm a gardener. I wish to nourish and protect, I know that there is beauty beneath the neglect.

-> Accept the pruning.
    <<jump Accept2>>
-> Refuse the pruning.
    <<jump Decline>>
===

title: Decline
---
<<bg thorn_layers_fullscreen>>
Narrator: She'd say go tend to elsewhere, I'm fending just fine. You can't tear down my defenses, you're wasting your time.
Narrator: For the receival of gifts she would not risk deceit. The gardener would step back, accepting defeat.
===

title: Accept2
---
<<bg dirt_and_trowel>>
Rose: You may remove just enough, but not a thorn more. Just an arm's gap of space, to allow you to pour.
Narrator: The gardener obeyed, much appeased by his feat. And she stayed on his mind as he made his retreat.
===